  "final_text": "I looked these up without changing anything.\n\n1. The 'Site health' dashboard has **2 panels**: \"Requests over time\" and \"Requests by response code\".\n2. The rule is called **Server errors**. It's an Elasticsearch query rule (`.es-query`). It is the only alert rule in Kibana. The lookup tool doesn't return a rule's query or index, so I couldn't confirm from its settings that it watches `kibana_sample_data_logs` for 5xx responses. Its name and the fact that no other rule exists point to it.\n3. It checks **every 1 minute**.\n4. It is **not enabled**. Because it's disabled, it isn't running, and its status shows \"pending\".\n\nPANELS: 2\nRULE_NAME: Server errors\nINTERVAL: 1m\nENABLED: no",
